    "# Section 1:  Dataset of known flash points\n",
    "\n",
    "The file `flash_point_data.csv` contains a dataset of known flash points for various solvents. In this section, you will examine this dataset and perform some basic analysis.\n",
    "\n",
    "In addition to compound names and flash points, the dataset contains the simplified molecular-input line-entry system (SMILES) of each molecule. SMILES are 1-D strings that allow you to present any small molecule in a character format. For example, propane can be written as `CCC`, where the capital C represents an sp3 hybridised carbon. In this part of the project, you will be looking at how to manipulate data in SMILES strings. You do not need to be an expert in SMILES to complete this part, but if you are interested in knowing more [here](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Simplified_molecular-input_line-entry_system) is a good starting point."
   ]
